tg_login_phone_hint = Enter your phone number in international format (e.g. +15551234567). Prefer Login with QR — phone codes rarely arrive for third-party apps.
tg_login_sms_note = Since 2023 Telegram does not send SMS login codes to third-party apps. Use Login with QR (scan from official Telegram → Devices), or enter an in-app code from an already logged-in official client.
tg_login_qr = Login with QR
tg_login_qr_hint = In official Telegram open Settings → Devices → Link Desktop Device and scan this code. Use split-screen or another phone/tablet. Stay on this screen until linked.
tg_open_devices = Open Telegram Devices
tg_add_account_phone = Add with phone number
tg_login_code_hint = Telegram accepted the send (status below). This is almost never SMS. Check official Telegram’s “Telegram” service chat on a device already logged into this number — or cancel and use Login with QR.
tg_login_phone_used = Code requested for
tg_login_code_stay = Keep this aNote screen open. Prefer switching to Login with QR if no code appears.
tg_open_telegram = Open Telegram (optional)
tg_resend_code = Resend / other method
tg_code_resent = Requested another delivery method.
tg_login_password_hint = Enter your Telegram two-step verification password.
tg_phone = Phone number
tg_code = Verification code
tg_password = 2FA password
tg_continue = Continue
tg_connecting = Connecting…
tg_type_message = Type a message…
tg_send = Send
tg_send_now = Send now
tg_schedule = Schedule
tg_schedule_at = Schedule at
tg_scheduled_ok = Scheduled for {0}
tg_schedule_invalid = Choose a future date and time
tg_schedule_cancel = Cancel schedule
tg_attach_file = Attach file
tg_attach_photo = Attach picture
tg_download = tap to download
tg_downloaded = Saved: {0}
